#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105588 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105730 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/id #uuid "3d38f3e0-4c27-5ac6-ac16-9c8f57e0000e" :question/math-academy-id "e-4327" :question/problem "Find the angle between $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 2,-1,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 1,5,-2 \\rangle$. Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 5+1\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{30}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos \\left( -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{6} \\right) \\approx 111.9^\\circ.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105589 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105731 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/id #uuid "d6d1be58-7321-50ca-a47d-5e80d55277c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-4328" :question/problem "Find $\\angle BAC$ given the points $A(2,-1,-5)$, $B(-1,0,-4)$, and $C(5,1,1).$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,-1,-5⟩,\\,b=⟨-1,0,-4⟩,\\,c=⟨5,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $\\triangle ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $\\angle BAC = \\theta.$\n\n![](images/28/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,-4⟩-⟨2,-1,-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,1,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨5,1,1⟩-⟨2,-1,-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,2,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 6}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{11}\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7\\sqrt{11}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos \\left( -\\dfrac{1}{7\\sqrt{11}} \\right) \\approx 92.5^\\circ.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105606 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/id #uuid "fb2df468-d70d-5300-8860-0cb729cb13c5" :question/math-academy-id "e-5112" :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot \\mathbf{b}=-4$, find the angle between $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle t, \\, -2 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 6, \\, t \\rangle$. Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "First, since $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot \\mathbf{b}=-4$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =-4 \\\\ t\\cdot 6+(-2)\\cdot t & =-4 \\\\ 6t-2t & =-4 \\\\ 4t & =-4 \\\\ t & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨-1,-2⟩,\\,b=⟨6,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{37}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{185}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos \\left( -\\dfrac{4}{\\sqrt{185}} \\right) \\approx 107.1^\\circ.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105730 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a8e4a99-a9c5-5fc7-9f78-396522052d4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{80.13}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236185} {:answer/id #uuid "586c1b66-72bd-5e5a-809f-ce7b04846d5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{83.21}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236374} {:answer/id #uuid "a9efda7a-7dc8-56d3-b172-0ab18dcb5157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{85.09}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236887} {:answer/id #uuid "cc0743c8-027e-5f13-a875-f054dcc036c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{77.11}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237112} {:answer/id #uuid "e813f475-9a7c-503d-b72f-d583e6e956a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{78.56}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a8e4a99-a9c5-5fc7-9f78-396522052d4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{80.13}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236185} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6595c31-e9b8-5500-bed2-a7809530f6dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237732}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5bb24474-02b6-5a79-8993-e3afc25833c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-101505" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 6+6\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{6}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{100}\\cdot \\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{10\\cdot 7} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{35}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{6}{35})≈{80.13}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237832 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105731 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "038e0307-c334-55eb-bdf7-692cdb33f023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235819} {:answer/id #uuid "1b828b15-9546-5cf0-85ab-65052d538e91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235988} {:answer/id #uuid "2f4453d6-d8fd-5271-b0b4-bfe00f1aacbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236116} {:answer/id #uuid "a55c473c-9e6a-53ad-a6d6-0755e21624d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236856} {:answer/id #uuid "af068867-e87c-56b9-9198-3ae81095df86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f4453d6-d8fd-5271-b0b4-bfe00f1aacbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236116} :answer-field/id #uuid "a361fc99-c6c3-5763-b077-11d54bd19f13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237654}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4443b852-41a5-5a76-994c-081bd2938800" :question/math-academy-id "q-101506" :question/problem "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(1,5,-1)$, $Q(5,1,1)$, and $R(2,5,0).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $P$, $Q$, $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨1,5,-1⟩,\\,q=⟨5,1,1⟩,\\,r=⟨2,5,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$ \n\n![](images/30/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨5,1,1⟩-⟨1,5,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-4,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨2,5,0⟩-⟨1,5,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{36}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})={45}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237837 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "279dbfad-79dc-50f6-b6fa-3ce7edf1161a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{180}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236066} {:answer/id #uuid "630a3920-ccb0-5a60-89f2-30f6fbcc0e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236444} {:answer/id #uuid "681203af-d4b1-51c3-94d0-513c563723ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{150}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236475} {:answer/id #uuid "df5de9da-72ad-5de5-a4ce-79bea1997639" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{135}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237221} {:answer/id #uuid "f1f6a6af-7ef5-5986-8844-e994ff9f43c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df5de9da-72ad-5de5-a4ce-79bea1997639" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{135}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237221} :answer-field/id #uuid "d525463c-b43a-5061-b33f-8f38a0b0c0cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "894928dd-75e2-52ce-a7a7-400cde0a1a19" :question/math-academy-id "q-101512" :question/problem "Given that $a\\cdot b=-5$, find the angle between $a=⟨2t,t⟩$ and $b=⟨1,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $a\\cdot b=-5$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =-5 \\\\ 2t\\cdot 1+t\\cdot 3 & =-5 \\\\ 2t+3t & =-5 \\\\ 5t & =-5 \\\\ t & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =⟨2(-1),\\,(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $a$ and $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{5\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})={135}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105731 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2862ca2a-adb7-5796-8313-b22d8a5b12ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{21}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257140} {:answer/id #uuid "39fe88fc-93ca-521b-9de0-d74cb48145ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{28}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257295} {:answer/id #uuid "b9f01669-27f7-5fea-8a72-da701fbefd3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258410} {:answer/id #uuid "bab64f78-e25b-5c79-be64-7b0e6eee1475" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{23}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258417} {:answer/id #uuid "c064f90f-d7fc-5ea2-ba2e-94db39898929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9f01669-27f7-5fea-8a72-da701fbefd3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258410} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cbe761b-522b-5c50-8f0e-7b60ad801f62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259219}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b0fe9fd8-6607-5b94-bf55-ff9abd1059dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-124826" :question/problem "Find $∠XZY$ given the points $X(-2,1,0)$, $Y(-1,0,4)$, and $Z(-1,2,-2).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $X$, $Y$, $Z$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=⟨-2,1,0⟩,\\,y=⟨-1,0,4⟩,\\,z=⟨-1,2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△XYZ$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠XZY=\\theta .$ \n\n![](images/87/87453fecb9da6b9e673ab5a85a289a3fac73f4fb90fc8f1b33e7c0a80b1ea77f.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ZX} & =x-z \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,0⟩-⟨-1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{ZY} & =y-z \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,4⟩-⟨-1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{ZX}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{ZY}}{|\\overset{\\to }{ZX}||\\overset{\\to }{ZY}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 6}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{40}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{240}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{4\\sqrt{15}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{15}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{15}})={25}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479836 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105730 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "159fd380-dce4-518a-a6d3-698ca5bb3eba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{12.5}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479391} {:answer/id #uuid "40b810eb-accf-5a4e-97d9-c8605d6d85e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{108.4}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479454} {:answer/id #uuid "a6d164bc-18d8-5190-a58a-7a02287b7760" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{61.3}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479608} {:answer/id #uuid "cd55f423-f72d-545f-ae08-9223b18ea389" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{114.4}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479673} {:answer/id #uuid "e31d771e-69db-5724-9462-443d78f7ca71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{46.9}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40b810eb-accf-5a4e-97d9-c8605d6d85e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{108.4}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479454} :answer-field/id #uuid "30fc2b81-3bdf-59c5-9db1-77618c2dc14a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479760}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0ffc2b95-6d99-59f1-9d71-68fe0c7010aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-18321" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=⟨1,-1,0⟩$ and $b=⟨0,1,-2⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot 1+0\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}})≈{108.4}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287913 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105730 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0daa6c22-b6f3-51d9-a6de-9fda6e8596b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{85.82}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284905} {:answer/id #uuid "1abecb7e-2e0a-5388-81ae-f79fa8d93b52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{79.76}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285026} {:answer/id #uuid "2ac816ad-f66f-5fc9-a2a3-07c82119d299" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{82.28}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285162} {:answer/id #uuid "69f3be6b-4783-52f4-84fe-9b95d561ffc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{94.32}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285757} {:answer/id #uuid "ee1020da-a591-5782-8a4a-25069e02b21f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{74.66}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0daa6c22-b6f3-51d9-a6de-9fda6e8596b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{85.82}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284905} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbf80208-e230-50e2-a705-9a72d129b4fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "213ad054-3594-5fcc-a936-bdc01a05c42f" :question/math-academy-id "q-19036" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=⟨4,-3,2⟩$ and $b=⟨3,4,1⟩.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 3+(-3)\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{29}\\cdot \\sqrt{26}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{754}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{754}})≈{85.82}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287925 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105731 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0810a2d0-0ce3-58a3-9628-07a5b6ebcc2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{54}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284850} {:answer/id #uuid "5624953c-3d14-5211-9d3b-b99bd07795e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{88}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285579} {:answer/id #uuid "928132bd-96e6-5295-82ca-5687c1d9b59a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{48}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286118} {:answer/id #uuid "a74373f1-aca2-51a2-8b3c-f754f55d3b95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{112}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286312} {:answer/id #uuid "d7340d34-1702-5e16-9dd2-b5e02a6027eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{18}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0810a2d0-0ce3-58a3-9628-07a5b6ebcc2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{54}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284850} :answer-field/id #uuid "50d04ce3-a358-500a-aed7-d670d76e14d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287326}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ea49a8dd-e4b2-55bc-b471-da1f1d77c574" :question/math-academy-id "q-19107" :question/problem "Find $∠BAC$ given the points $A(2,1,-1)$, $B(3,-2,2)$, and $C(-1,-2,1).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,1,-1⟩,\\,b=⟨3,-2,2⟩,\\,c=⟨-1,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](images/28/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,2⟩-⟨2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩-⟨2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-3,2⟩\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{19}\\cdot \\sqrt{22}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{418}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{418}})≈{54}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106109 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0062f752-bd13-50a8-bb70-b3e95306d293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{48.72}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479356} {:answer/id #uuid "658fb7cc-1f50-5aa6-b7c7-ebf465725a6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{71.57}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479508} {:answer/id #uuid "73751b94-0fcf-518d-b94d-26000db59887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{78.37}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479533} {:answer/id #uuid "c74b2731-625c-5686-9738-6b4cb96f3c7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{63.28}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479661} {:answer/id #uuid "f94a9a14-2446-5ad2-a0a9-1e0bdc5cf916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{105.61}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "658fb7cc-1f50-5aa6-b7c7-ebf465725a6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{71.57}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479508} :answer-field/id #uuid "589c07ef-1c36-566e-ab30-36c2c2bba507" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102530}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4e1c8f13-f8d5-58eb-9a61-227e3239a680" :question/math-academy-id "q-19115" :question/problem "Consider the points $A(t,2,1)$, $B(2t,3,1)$ and $C(2,{t}^{2},-1).$ Find $∠BAC$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=2.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨t,\\,2,\\,1⟩,\\,b=⟨2t,\\,3,\\,1⟩,\\,c=⟨2,\\,{t}^{2},\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](images/28/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,3,\\,1⟩-⟨t,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,{t}^{2},\\,-1⟩-⟨t,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2-t,\\,{t}^{2}-2,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=2$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =2 \\\\ t\\cdot (2-t)+1\\cdot ({t}^{2}-2)+0\\cdot (-2) & =2 \\\\ 2t-{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}-2+0 & =2 \\\\ 2t-2 & =2 \\\\ 2t & =4 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨2,1,0⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨2-2,\\,{2}^{2}-2,\\,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{8}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2\\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}})≈{71.57}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287926 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "079ab0d0-3cbc-5082-b6ab-365990a42e59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{93.32}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284845} {:answer/id #uuid "2289598c-d338-5f6b-9292-973ab0684d4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{81.64}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285098} {:answer/id #uuid "34289431-f128-575f-97c2-e4e6f94e3262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{88.29}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285268} {:answer/id #uuid "83273044-960b-5f85-92e0-995f1a281dc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{52.15}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285991} {:answer/id #uuid "d4cd56ba-92df-53d0-857a-cb0a2bbe1247" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{67.48}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2289598c-d338-5f6b-9292-973ab0684d4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{81.64}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285098} :answer-field/id #uuid "acb00cac-bbd3-5fdd-ada8-fc80dcbf1675" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287502}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "567d9479-bc13-5331-b757-cfe1cd8387a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-19119" :question/problem "Consider the points $D(1,3,2)$, $E(t,2,4)$ and $F(3,t,3).$ Find $∠EDF$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF}=2.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $D$, $E$, $F$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d=⟨1,\\,3,\\,2⟩,\\,e=⟨t,\\,2,\\,4⟩,\\,f=⟨3,\\,t,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△DEF$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠EDF=\\theta .$\n\n![](images/c9/c9cfb3e84e6f76d243125f2a09246b2a1300a0134e71359bb2b528082f064f93.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =e-d \\\\  & =⟨t,\\,2,\\,4⟩-⟨1,\\,3,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t-1,\\,-1,\\,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =f-d \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,t,\\,3⟩-⟨1,\\,3,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,t-3,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF}=2$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =2 \\\\ (t-1)\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (t-3)+2\\cdot 1 & =2 \\\\ 2t-2-t+3+2 & =2 \\\\ t & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =⟨-1-1,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,-1,2⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =⟨2,-1-3,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-4,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF}}{|\\overset{\\to }{DE}||\\overset{\\to }{DF}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{21}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{21}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{21}})≈{81.64}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335941 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105730 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a54a649-fdd6-5ec4-81c1-25723a4e2136" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{47.1}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334088} {:answer/id #uuid "7f5f592b-b2ff-5354-ba44-ead6aacd04f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{42.3}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334124} {:answer/id #uuid "9d5d594c-a35e-5f05-ae4a-f5df1b11088f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{31.7}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334376} {:answer/id #uuid "c84d6cb4-2cee-52fa-8de6-0a9379c6bd3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{35.6}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334731} {:answer/id #uuid "ed12f6a1-dfc9-5ed6-835b-c48fbee37dc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45.3}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c84d6cb4-2cee-52fa-8de6-0a9379c6bd3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{35.6}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334731} :answer-field/id #uuid "06db28a8-7c01-5bb4-9c2d-52d54418cb29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335246}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aa6fe310-eeef-5a18-a61a-06fedd1010e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-67797" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=⟨-1,7,0⟩$ and $b=⟨3,6,-1⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 3+7\\cdot 6+0\\cdot (-1)}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{7}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{\\sqrt{50}\\cdot \\sqrt{46}} \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{\\sqrt{2300}} \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{10\\sqrt{23}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{39}{10\\sqrt{23}})≈{35.6}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336007 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105731 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "382cb607-2c08-5d7e-a967-c6d75cc084f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333509} {:answer/id #uuid "3e71dcdb-a48d-57d3-a1bd-cdac86069077" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333578} {:answer/id #uuid "5927a3fa-7ca4-5835-8996-fbb98d090ec9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{180}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333805} {:answer/id #uuid "690b7cff-b32c-5363-bd25-f017d4b42be0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333952} {:answer/id #uuid "c20e456b-f54c-5860-ac8e-9965a8df1f0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5927a3fa-7ca4-5835-8996-fbb98d090ec9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{180}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333805} :answer-field/id #uuid "daa4074b-77d0-50c6-a0c2-ed91e9092a62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335627}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "06345d34-3e03-5708-b180-d74d0f414ffb" :question/math-academy-id "q-69828" :question/problem "Find $∠PQR$ given the points $P(-3,0,-1)$, $Q(-1,1,0)$, and $R(1,2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $P$, $Q$, $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨-3,0,-1⟩,\\,q=⟨-1,1,0⟩,\\,r=⟨1,2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠PQR=\\theta .$ \n\n![](images/20/209d43a5aab5d57fbd4cd7b421d41f0fa85bc58cfdd36251a8acf392b0ba7312.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{QP}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{QR}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QP} & =p-q \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,-1⟩-⟨-1,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{QR} & =r-q \\\\  & =⟨1,2,1⟩-⟨-1,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{QP}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{QR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{QP}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{QR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{QP}||\\overset{\\to }{QR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-1)={180}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336010 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105731 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "321940d9-bd6b-529f-b36b-52de6034ea1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333452} {:answer/id #uuid "47c034fd-ff2c-563e-807c-0bd209a7f45d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333653} {:answer/id #uuid "5d29e042-7c4a-5adf-9528-5bd45b78ba7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333842} {:answer/id #uuid "7fc9f4bc-7a23-5d72-9079-6503dce5faa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334126} {:answer/id #uuid "c99908af-2c65-5635-a798-8ecd8753f621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fc9f4bc-7a23-5d72-9079-6503dce5faa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334126} :answer-field/id #uuid "e443c3bb-f95f-5b04-a2c2-a7d665f716b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335635}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1615350f-44ad-5e4b-849c-6c410f4c58d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-69833" :question/problem "Find $∠XZY$ given the points $X(-1,0,3)$, $Y(-2,2,3)$, and $Z(-2,-1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $X$, $Y$, $Z$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=⟨-1,0,3⟩,\\,y=⟨-2,2,3⟩,\\,z=⟨-2,-1,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△XYZ$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠XZY=\\theta .$ \n\n![](images/87/87453fecb9da6b9e673ab5a85a289a3fac73f4fb90fc8f1b33e7c0a80b1ea77f.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ZX} & =x-z \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,3⟩-⟨-2,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{ZY} & =y-z \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,3⟩-⟨-2,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,3,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{ZX}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{ZY}}{|\\overset{\\to }{ZX}||\\overset{\\to }{ZY}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})={45}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479850 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105730 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02cb6fee-ce7d-560e-8ed7-f39aa200d67d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479364} {:answer/id #uuid "1c69ef4d-faaf-5822-b026-b326887faa8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{135}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479404} {:answer/id #uuid "52500d10-896d-510b-8140-363810b9ef46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{150}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479478} {:answer/id #uuid "e01fccff-bbff-54ab-98f2-ea5e909b0798" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479690} {:answer/id #uuid "ebf08a51-4f87-56eb-a1bf-608bbb2ea4f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{180}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02cb6fee-ce7d-560e-8ed7-f39aa200d67d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479364} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2059258-9233-559a-842c-f610002a589b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4a507c40-e9a1-5cff-8a8b-72e01c23590f" :question/math-academy-id "q-69909" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot (-1)+0\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})={120}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345280 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00e6e668-b82c-5f64-b7e7-a49b270c95a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{58}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342251} {:answer/id #uuid "3869e1bb-0ad4-52cb-a463-44a68621aede" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{79}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342702} {:answer/id #uuid "a3adb946-e512-55eb-a187-ced61f86a274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{65}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343679} {:answer/id #uuid "c10fdcde-262c-592d-97e1-748297e33ae3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{75}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343934} {:answer/id #uuid "d0600b8a-b989-5d6f-b12e-8260c9aaac01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{82}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c10fdcde-262c-592d-97e1-748297e33ae3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{75}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343934} :answer-field/id #uuid "cce7cda2-b89f-5700-a5ff-e0aac43f4d18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b5e4f513-9065-59e2-89d1-49300cc3f2d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-77164" :question/problem "Consider the points $A(3t,t,4),$ $B(3t,4t,3)$ and $C(5t,t+1,5).$ Find $∠BAC$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=2.$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩,\\,b=⟨3t,\\,4t,\\,3⟩,\\,c=⟨5t,\\,t+1,\\,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](images/28/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3t,\\,4t,\\,3⟩-⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,3t,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨5t,\\,t+1,\\,5⟩-⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=2$, we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =2 \\\\ 0\\cdot 2t+3t\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 1 & =2 \\\\ 3t-1 & =2 \\\\ 3t & =3 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨0,3,-1⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨2,\\,1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{10}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2\\sqrt{15}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{15}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{15}})≈{75}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345282 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "076d4f2b-e206-5510-92ce-4af922c0cfe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{21.42}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342302} {:answer/id #uuid "09c10234-682a-51c0-848d-206b08c9c6d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{10.52}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342319} {:answer/id #uuid "65b42fb4-c57a-5acb-8b41-1a6bc8e50526" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{77.07}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343100} {:answer/id #uuid "8da02dc4-e6c4-5060-a581-992098de8461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{63.43}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343477} {:answer/id #uuid "8f319fd7-e716-51df-a6fb-e0a06bd1cd90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{26.57}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f319fd7-e716-51df-a6fb-e0a06bd1cd90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{26.57}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343492} :answer-field/id #uuid "453dd8cb-e3c7-57eb-bb1b-6f649dd1458a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344607}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2aca6a5f-5821-5a6c-aed6-f1272cbcca9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-77167" :question/problem "Consider the points $A(2t,4,3),$ $B(5t-1,4,3)$ and $C(2t+4,t+5,3).$ Find $∠BAC$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=8.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2t,\\,4,\\,3⟩,\\,b=⟨5t-1,\\,4,\\,3⟩,\\,c=⟨2t+4,\\,t+5,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](images/28/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨5t-1,\\,4,\\,3⟩-⟨2t,\\,4,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3t-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨2t+4,\\,t+5,\\,3⟩-⟨2t,\\,4,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,t+1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=8,$ we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =8 \\\\ (3t-1)\\cdot 4+0\\cdot (t+1)+0\\cdot 0 & =8 \\\\ 4(3t-1)+0+0 & =8 \\\\ 12t-4 & =8 \\\\ 12t & =12 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨2,0,0⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨4,\\,2,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{80}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{4\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}})≈{26.57}^{∘}.\n$$"}]}
